IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XII -- Shareholders: lists, quorum, voting,
-- written resolutions (ss 138 to 142).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. Where a section says "unless the
-- by-laws otherwise provide" (or the articles), the rule takes an input saying whether they do, and
-- answers the question "does the statutory default apply"; when they do, the by-laws govern and the
-- default answer is FALSE (or NOTHING), not a guess about what the by-laws say. A record date computed in
-- the meetings module (s 134) is a plain DATE input here. Regulations are not a source: "in accordance
-- with the regulations, if any" is a plain BOOLEAN. Dates: Part XII holds no enactment, assent or
-- commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XII -- Shareholders: lists, quorum, voting, written resolutions (ss 138 to 142)`

§§ `s 138(1) -- the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice`

-- Ten days after a record date fixed for receiving notice: the day of the record date is day 0 and the tenth
-- day after it is in time (the keel's convention, fork F1).
-- src:1728 | (a) if a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), not later than ten days after that date; or
@ref CBCA s 138(1)(a) (src:1728)
`the ten days of s 138` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- (1) A corporation shall prepare an alphabetical list of its shareholders entitled to receive notice of a
-- meeting, showing the number of shares held by each, (a) if a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c),
-- not later than ten days after that date; or (b) if no record date is fixed, ON the record date established
-- under paragraph 134(2)(a) (fork F-138-1b: "on" is the day, and a different word from (3)'s "not later than").
-- The relation: the shareholders entitled to receive notice are owed the list; the corporation owes it.
-- src:1727 | 138 (1) A corporation shall prepare an alphabetical list of its shareholders entitled to receive notice of a meeting, showing the number of shares held by each shareholder,
-- src:1728 | (a) if a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), not later than ten days after that date; or
-- src:1729 | (b) if no record date is fixed, on the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a).
@ref CBCA s 138(1) (src:1727-1729)
GIVEN `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to prepare the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice within s 138(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed`
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN `the last day of` `the ten days of s 138` `counted from` fixed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)`

@ref CBCA s 138(1) (src:1727-1729)
GIVEN `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE
      `the date the list was prepared` IS A DATE
      `the list is alphabetical` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice complies with s 138(1)` MEANS
        `the list is alphabetical`
    AND `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder`
    AND CONSIDER `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed`
        WHEN JUST fixed THEN `done within the time limit` `the ten days of s 138` fixed `the date the list was prepared`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the list was prepared` EQUALS `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)`

§§ `s 138(2), (3) -- the list of shareholders entitled to vote`

-- (2) If a record date for voting is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d), the list of shareholders entitled to vote as
-- of that date is prepared no later than ten days after it. (3) If no record date for voting is fixed, it is
-- prepared not later than ten days after the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c) or, if none, not later
-- than the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a), "as the case may be".
-- src:1730 | Voting list — if record date fixed
-- src:1731 | (2) If a record date for voting is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d), the corporation shall prepare, no later than ten days after the record date, an alphabetical list of shareholders entitled to vote as of the record date at a meeting of shareholders that shows the number of shares held by each shareholder.
-- src:1732 | Voting list — if no record date fixed
-- src:1733 | (3) If a record date for voting is not fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d), the corporation shall prepare, not later than 10 days after the record date that is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c) or not later than the record date that is established under paragraph 134(2)(a), as the case may be, an alphabetical list of shareholders who are entitled to vote as of the record date that shows the number of shares held by each shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 138(2) and (3) (src:1730-1733)
GIVEN `the record date for voting fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d), if one is fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to prepare the list of shareholders entitled to vote within s 138(2) and (3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the record date for voting fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d), if one is fixed`
    WHEN JUST voting THEN `the last day of` `the ten days of s 138` `counted from` voting
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed`
        WHEN JUST fixed THEN `the last day of` `the ten days of s 138` `counted from` fixed
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)`

@ref CBCA s 138(2) and (3) (src:1731 src:1733)
GIVEN `the record date for voting fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d), if one is fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE
      `the date the list was prepared` IS A DATE
      `the list is alphabetical` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the list of shareholders entitled to vote complies with s 138(2) and (3)` MEANS
        `the list is alphabetical`
    AND `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder`
    AND `the date the list was prepared` AT MOST (`the last day to prepare the list of shareholders entitled to vote within s 138(2) and (3)` `the record date for voting fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d), if one is fixed` `the record date fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c), if one is fixed` `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)`)

-- (3.1) A shareholder whose name appears on a list prepared under (2) or (3) is entitled to vote the shares shown
-- opposite their name at the meeting to which the list relates. The section says nothing about a shareholder whose
-- name does not appear, so that case is NOTHING, not nought shares.
-- src:1735 | (3.1) A shareholder whose name appears on a list prepared under subsection (2) or (3) is entitled to vote the shares shown opposite their name at the meeting to which the list relates.
@ref CBCA s 138(3.1) (src:1735)
GIVEN `the shareholder's name appears on a list prepared under subsection 138(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares shown opposite the shareholder's name` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the shares the shareholder may vote at the meeting within s 138(3.1)` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder's name appears on a list prepared under subsection 138(2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST `the number of shares shown opposite the shareholder's name`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 138(4) -- examination of the list`

-- A shareholder may examine the list (a) during usual business hours at the registered office of the corporation
-- or at the place where its central securities register is maintained; and (b) at the meeting for which the list
-- was prepared. The two are alternative occasions ("and" joins the two occasions on which the right exists, not
-- two conditions of one occasion).
-- src:1737 | (4) A shareholder may examine the list of shareholders
-- src:1738 | (a) during usual business hours at the registered office of the corporation or at the place where its central securities register is maintained; and
-- src:1739 | (b) at the meeting of shareholders for which the list was prepared.
@ref CBCA s 138(4) (src:1737-1739)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is during usual business hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is at the registered office of the corporation or at the place where its central securities register is maintained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is at the meeting of shareholders for which the list was prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a shareholder may examine the list within s 138(4)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder`
    AND (    (    `it is during usual business hours`
              AND `it is at the registered office of the corporation or at the place where its central securities register is maintained`)
         OR  `it is at the meeting of shareholders for which the list was prepared`)

§§ `s 139 -- quorum`

-- (1) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, a quorum of shareholders is present, irrespective of the number of
-- persons actually present, if the holders of a MAJORITY of the shares entitled to vote are present in person or
-- represented by proxy. A majority is more than half: exactly half is not a majority (fork F-139-tie). Where the
-- by-laws otherwise provide, their rule is a plain input.
-- src:1741 | 139 (1) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, a quorum of shareholders is present at a meeting of shareholders, irrespective of the number of persons actually present at the meeting, if the holders of a majority of the shares entitled to vote at the meeting are present in person or represented by proxy.
@ref CBCA s 139(1) (src:1741)
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the quorum the by-laws provide is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting held by those present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a quorum of shareholders is present within s 139(1)` MEANS
    IF `the by-laws otherwise provide`
    THEN `the quorum the by-laws provide is present`
    ELSE 2 TIMES `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting held by those present in person or represented by proxy` GREATER THAN `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting`

-- (2) If a quorum is present at the opening, the shareholders present may, unless the by-laws otherwise provide,
-- proceed with the business although a quorum is not present throughout.
-- src:1743 | (2) If a quorum is present at the opening of a meeting of shareholders, the shareholders present may, unless the by-laws otherwise provide, proceed with the business of the meeting, notwithstanding that a quorum is not present throughout the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 139(2) (src:1743)
GIVEN `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders present may proceed with the business within s 139(2)` MEANS
        `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting`
    AND (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)

-- (3) If a quorum is not present at the opening, the shareholders present may adjourn the meeting to a fixed time
-- and place but may not transact any other business. Where a quorum IS present the subsection is silent.
-- src:1745 | (3) If a quorum is not present at the opening of a meeting of shareholders, the shareholders present may adjourn the meeting to a fixed time and place but may not transact any other business.
@ref CBCA s 139(3) (src:1745)
GIVEN `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders present may adjourn the meeting to a fixed time and place within s 139(3)` MEANS
    (NOT `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting`)

@ref CBCA s 139(3) (src:1745)
GIVEN `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the shareholders present may transact other business within s 139(3)` MEANS
    IF `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (4) If a corporation has only one shareholder, or only one holder of any class or series of shares, the
-- shareholder present in person or by proxy constitutes a meeting.
-- src:1747 | (4) If a corporation has only one shareholder, or only one holder of any class or series of shares, the shareholder present in person or by proxy constitutes a meeting.
@ref CBCA s 139(4) (src:1747)
GIVEN `the corporation has only one shareholder, or only one holder of the class or series of shares in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that shareholder is present in person or by proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder present constitutes a meeting within s 139(4)` MEANS
        `the corporation has only one shareholder, or only one holder of the class or series of shares in question`
    AND `that shareholder is present in person or by proxy`

§§ `s 140 -- the right to vote`

-- (1) Unless the articles otherwise provide, each share entitles the holder to one vote at a meeting of
-- shareholders. Where the articles otherwise provide, the votes per share are what they provide; absent that
-- input, NOTHING. The relation: the shareholder holds the claim to the votes; the corporation the duty to count them.
-- src:1749 | 140 (1) Unless the articles otherwise provide, each share of a corporation entitles the holder thereof to one vote at a meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 140(1) (src:1749)
GIVEN `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes per share the articles provide, if they provide otherwise` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the votes each share carries within s 140(1)` MEANS
    IF `the articles otherwise provide`
    THEN `the votes per share the articles provide, if they provide otherwise`
    ELSE JUST 1

@ref CBCA s 140(1) (src:1749)
GIVEN `the number of shares the holder holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes each share carries` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the votes a holder may cast within s 140(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the votes each share carries`
    WHEN JUST each THEN JUST (`the number of shares the holder holds` TIMES each)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (2) If a body corporate or association is a shareholder, the corporation shall recognize any individual
-- authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body of the body corporate or association to represent
-- it at meetings of shareholders. (3) That individual may exercise on its behalf all the powers it could exercise if
-- it were an individual shareholder.
-- src:1751 | (2) If a body corporate or association is a shareholder of a corporation, the corporation shall recognize any individual authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body of the body corporate or association to represent it at meetings of shareholders of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 140(2) (src:1751)
GIVEN `the shareholder is a body corporate or association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body of the body corporate or association to represent it at meetings of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must recognize the individual as the representative within s 140(2)` MEANS
        `the shareholder is a body corporate or association`
    AND `the individual is authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body of the body corporate or association to represent it at meetings of shareholders`

-- src:1753 | (3) An individual authorized under subsection (2) may exercise on behalf of the body corporate or association all the powers it could exercise if it were an individual shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 140(3) (src:1753)
GIVEN `the individual is authorized under subsection 140(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the representative may exercise all the powers of an individual shareholder within s 140(3)` MEANS
    `the individual is authorized under subsection 140(2)`

-- (4) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, if two or more persons hold shares jointly, one of those holders present
-- at a meeting may in the absence of the others vote the shares; but if two or more of them who are present, in
-- person or by proxy, vote, they shall vote as one on the shares jointly held. (The count of joint holders is the
-- caller's; counting joint holders as one holder is for the Part XIII rules, ss 149(2) and 150(1.1).)
-- src:1755 | (4) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, if two or more persons hold shares jointly, one of those holders present at a meeting of shareholders may in the absence of the others vote the shares, but if two or more of those persons who are present, in person or by proxy, vote, they shall vote as one on the shares jointly held by them.
@ref CBCA s 140(4) (src:1755)
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of those holders present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`one joint holder present may vote the shares in the absence of the others within s 140(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons`
    AND `the number of those holders present at the meeting` EQUALS 1

@ref CBCA s 140(4) (src:1755)
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of those holders who are present, in person or by proxy, and who vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the joint holders who vote must vote as one within s 140(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons`
    AND `the number of those holders who are present, in person or by proxy, and who vote` AT LEAST 2

§§ `s 141 -- voting`

-- (1) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, voting at a meeting is by show of hands except where a ballot is
-- demanded by a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote at the meeting.
-- src:1757 | 141 (1) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, voting at a meeting of shareholders shall be by show of hands except where a ballot is demanded by a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 141(1) (src:1757)
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ballot is demanded by a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`voting is by show of hands within s 141(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND (NOT `a ballot is demanded by a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote at the meeting`)

-- (2) A shareholder or proxyholder may demand a ballot either before or after any vote by show of hands.
-- (1) says the demander is one "entitled to vote at the meeting"; (2) does not (finding 18 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1759 | (2) A shareholder or proxyholder may demand a ballot either before or after any vote by show of hands.
@ref CBCA s 141(2) (src:1759)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder or proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is made before or after a vote by show of hands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a ballot may be demanded within s 141(2)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder or proxyholder`
    AND `the demand is made before or after a vote by show of hands`

-- (3) Despite (1), unless the by-laws otherwise provide, any vote in (1) may be held, in accordance with the
-- regulations, if any, entirely by a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, if the corporation
-- makes such a facility available.
-- src:1761 | (3) Despite subsection (1), unless the by-laws otherwise provide, any vote referred to in subsection (1) may be held, in accordance with the regulations, if any, entirely by means of a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, if the corporation makes available such a communication facility.
@ref CBCA s 141(3) (src:1761)
GIVEN `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation makes a communication facility available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote is held in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a vote may be held entirely by electronic means within s 141(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND `the corporation makes a communication facility available`
    AND `the vote is held in accordance with the regulations, if any`

-- (4) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, a person participating in a meeting under s 132(4) or (5) and entitled
-- to vote may vote, in accordance with the regulations, if any, by the facility the corporation has made available
-- for that purpose.
-- src:1763 | (4) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, any person participating in a meeting of shareholders under subsection 132(4) or (5) and entitled to vote at that meeting may vote, in accordance with the regulations, if any, by means of the telephonic, electronic or other communication facility that the corporation has made available for that purpose.
@ref CBCA s 141(4) (src:1763)
GIVEN `the person participates in the meeting under subsection 132(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has made a communication facility available for voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote is cast in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a participant may vote by the facility within s 141(4)` MEANS
        `the person participates in the meeting under subsection 132(4) or (5)`
    AND `the person is entitled to vote at the meeting`
    AND (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND `the corporation has made a communication facility available for voting`
    AND `the vote is cast in accordance with the regulations, if any`

§§ `s 142 -- resolutions in lieu of a meeting`

-- (1) Except where a written statement is submitted by a director under s 110(2) or by an auditor under s 168(5),
-- (a) a resolution in writing signed by ALL the shareholders entitled to vote on it at a meeting is as valid as if
-- passed at a meeting; and (b) a resolution in writing dealing with all matters required by the Act to be dealt
-- with at a meeting, and signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting, satisfies all the
-- requirements of the Act relating to meetings. The s 110(2) statement is a director's (out of range: section 110,
-- the directors' piece); the s 168(5) statement is the auditor's (own range, Part XIV): both are plain inputs.
-- src:1765 | 142 (1) Except where a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2) or by an auditor under subsection 168(5),
-- src:1766 | (a) a resolution in writing signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on that resolution at a meeting of shareholders is as valid as if it had been passed at a meeting of the shareholders; and
@ref CBCA s 142(1)(a) (src:1765-1766)
GIVEN `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a written resolution is as valid as if passed at a meeting within s 142(1)(a)` MEANS
        (NOT `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)`)
    AND (NOT `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)`)
    AND `the resolution is in writing`
    AND `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it at a meeting of shareholders`

-- src:1765 | 142 (1) Except where a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2) or by an auditor under subsection 168(5),
-- src:1766 | (a) a resolution in writing signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on that resolution at a meeting of shareholders is as valid as if it had been passed at a meeting of the shareholders; and
-- src:1767 | (b) a resolution in writing dealing with all matters required by this Act to be dealt with at a meeting of shareholders, and signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting, satisfies all the requirements of this Act relating to meetings of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 142(1)(b) (src:1765 src:1767)
GIVEN `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution deals with all matters required by the Act to be dealt with at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a written resolution satisfies the requirements relating to meetings within s 142(1)(b)` MEANS
        (NOT `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)`)
    AND (NOT `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)`)
    AND `the resolution is in writing`
    AND `the resolution deals with all matters required by the Act to be dealt with at a meeting of shareholders`
    AND `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting`

-- (2) A copy of every resolution referred to in (1) shall be kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders.
-- The relation: the shareholders and the Director (who may inspect records, a matter outside this range) are owed the
-- keeping; the corporation owes it.
-- src:1769 | (2) A copy of every resolution referred to in subsection (1) shall be kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 142(2) (src:1769)
GIVEN `the resolution is one referred to in subsection 142(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must keep a copy of the resolution with the minutes within s 142(2)` MEANS
    `the resolution is one referred to in subsection 142(1)`

@ref CBCA s 142(2) (src:1769)
GIVEN `the corporation must keep a copy of the resolution with the minutes within s 142(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy is kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to keep a copy of the resolution is met within s 142(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must keep a copy of the resolution with the minutes within s 142(2)`)
    OR  `a copy is kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders`

-- (3) Unless a ballot is demanded, an entry in the minutes of a meeting that the chairperson declared a resolution
-- carried or defeated is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the fact without proof of the number
-- or proportion of votes. The rule says whether the entry stands as proof; evidence to the contrary rebuts it.
-- src:1771 | (3) Unless a ballot is demanded, an entry in the minutes of a meeting to the effect that the chairperson of the meeting declared a resolution to be carried or defeated is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the fact without proof of the number or proportion of the votes recorded in favour of or against the resolution.
@ref CBCA s 142(3) (src:1771)
GIVEN `a ballot is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minutes of the meeting have an entry that the chairperson of the meeting declared a resolution to be carried or defeated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the minutes entry is proof of the declaration within s 142(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `a ballot is demanded`)
    AND `the minutes of the meeting have an entry that the chairperson of the meeting declared a resolution to be carried or defeated`
    AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
